{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "name": "Ecommerce API v1",
    "description": "Documentation and testing collection for the ecommerce API.\n\n### How to use\n1. Start the server with `npm run dev`.\n2. Run `Register User`, then promote that email to admin in PostgreSQL:\n\n```sql\nUPDATE users SET role = 'admin' WHERE email = '<the registered email>';\n```\n\n3. Run `Login`; the JWT is saved to `token`.\n4. Run `Create Category`, then `Create Product`.\n5. Guest reads such as `Get All Products` do not need a token.\n6. Cart and address requests need the same `{{token}}`. A regular user token is enough; admin is not required.\n7. Try deleting a category before deleting its product to see a `409 Conflict` response.\n8. Delete the product, then delete the category.\n\n### Access\n- Public: register, login, and all catalog GET requests (guest browsing).\n- Authenticated: `GET /auth/me`, all cart requests, and all address requests.\n- Admin: category and product create, update, and delete.\n\n### Notes\n- All requests use `{{baseUrl}}`.\n- Write, cart, and address requests send `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`.\n- `slug`, `ratingAverage`, and `ratingsCount` are server-owned and are not accepted on create or update.\n- Price is sent as `priceInMinorUnits` — an integer in the smallest currency unit.\n- Adding to the cart does not decrease stock. Stock is checked only so quantity cannot exceed what is available.\n- Phone numbers must be Saudi: `05XXXXXXXX` or `+9665XXXXXXXX`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Base URL for the local server."
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Saved automatically after a successful `Login` request."
    },
    {
      "key": "userEmail",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Saved automatically after a successful `Register User` request."
    },
    {
      "key": "userPassword",
      "value": "Secret123!",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Password used by the Auth requests in this collection."
    },
    {
      "key": "categoryId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Saved automatically after a successful `Create Category` request."
    },
    {
      "key": "productId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Saved automatically after a successful `Create Product` request."
    },
    {
      "key": "cartItemId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Saved automatically after a successful add or update cart item request."
    },
    {
      "key": "addressId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Saved automatically after a successful create or update address request."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "Register and login. Catalog writes need an admin token. New accounts start as `user`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.data?.user?.email) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('userEmail', json.data.user.email);",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Password hash is not returned', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(json.data.user.passwordHash).to.be.undefined;",
                  "  pm.expect(json.data.user.password).to.be.undefined;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman User\",\n  \"email\": \"postman.{{$timestamp}}@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Creates a `user` account and saves `email` to `userEmail`.\n\nThe response never includes `password` or `passwordHash`.\n\nTo use catalog write requests, promote the user in PostgreSQL then run `Login`:\n\n```sql\nUPDATE users SET role = 'admin' WHERE email = '<registered email>';\n```"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.data?.token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', json.data.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Signs in and saves the JWT to `token`.\n\nIf you promoted the user to `admin`, log in again so the token includes the new role.\n\nWrong email or password returns `401` with `Invalid email or password`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Me",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the current user from the access token.\n\n- Missing or invalid token: `401`.\n- The response never includes `passwordHash`."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
